# DTF tier manifest: upload-staging-object-store-single-put
#   artifact-keeper#3916 (single-PUT remainder): a single PUT into an
#   object-storage repository streams its body to the repository's backend
#   with bounded memory instead of spooling it to local scratch, for the
#   generic route and for Maven.
#   Profile-set: storage.s3 (MinIO) + scratch.readonly (AK_UPLOAD_STAGING_DIR
#   on an empty read-only volume, so any upload that spools fails).
#   Sibling of upload-staging-object-store (raw PUT, multipart, chunked).
#
# THE GAP
#   The generic PUT has staged on the repository's backend since 1.11.0
#   (#4321), but the Maven PUT still spooled every jar, POM and checksum
#   sidecar to a scratch file under AK_UPLOAD_STAGING_DIR before writing it
#   to S3, so a Maven deploy needed local disk the size of its largest jar and
#   failed outright (503 upload_spool_failed) when that disk was full or
#   read-only.
#
# Gates:
#   (CONTROL, both images) a 40 MiB generic PUT answers 201 and downloads
#   byte-identical (it already streams).
#   (FIX) a 40 MiB Maven jar, its POM and the jar's .sha1 sidecar PUT through
#   the Maven route answer 201; the jar downloads byte-identical; the POM's
#   metadata is recorded; no generic-upload-staging object or tracking row is
#   left once the uploads finish.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: back-to-back uploads.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5. Green: ak-backend:lane-w3a.
PROFILES="storage.s3 scratch.readonly"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
